            {
              "id": "gid://gitlab/Discussion/49b43441a91935de00573fe223b5e03165d9615a",
              "resolvable": false,
              "resolved": false,
              "notes": {
                "pageInfo": {
                  "hasNextPage": false
                },
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "id": "gid://gitlab/Note/4101193028",
                    "body": "This is a well-tested, carefully engineered change: the systemd/launchd config parsers and the atomic-write/rollback logic in `Install` are covered by extensive table-driven tests that match documented systemd/launchd semantics, and I could not find a defect in the core parsing (`systemdServiceValues`, `systemdWords`, `systemdUnescape`, `plistEnv`) or in the removal/rollback flow (`writeUnits`, `removeUnloaded`), which I traced in detail against their tests.\n\nI did find one gap worth a look: `installFallbackSync` in `setup.go` writes `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` into the job without validating it is an absolute path, even though the existing `claudehooks.CheckConfigDir()` helper does that check for the hooks path and `InstalledClaudeConfigDir` itself rejects a relative value when read back — so a relative `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` could be silently written into the job. I also flagged a narrower, lower-confidence inconsistency where `readJob`'s fixed-path existence check can short-circuit before `systemdServiceFiles`'s broader directory search runs.",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-27T17:19:15Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": "2026-10-27T17:19:17Z",
                    "url": "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4230#note_4101193028",
                    "system": false,
                    "internal": false,
                    "author": {
                      "username": "GitLabDuo",
                      "name": "GitLab Duo",
                      "avatarUrl": "/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836",
                      "bot": true
                    },
                    "position": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "gid://gitlab/Discussion/b4c66a25c1d2b2dc270b35ddd3497a6ed6f4eecb",
              "resolvable": true,
              "resolved": true,
              "notes": {
                "pageInfo": {
                  "hasNextPage": false
                },
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "id": "gid://gitlab/DiffNote/4101192900",
                    "body": "`readJob` only checks the single, fixed path `Units(goos, home, Job{})[0].Path` (i.e. `~/.config/systemd/user/glab-govern-audit-sync.service` on Linux) and returns `ErrNotInstalled` if that exact file is missing. `InstalledBinary` and `InstalledClaudeConfigDir` call `readJob` first and bail out with `ErrNotInstalled` before ever calling `systemdServiceFiles`, which searches the full systemd user unit directory priority list (`user.control`, `/etc/systemd/user`, etc.). So if the service unit lives in one of those higher-priority directories but not in `~/.config/systemd/user`, both functions report `ErrNotInstalled` even though `systemdServiceFiles` would have found it. This is a narrow edge case (glab always installs to `~/.config/systemd/user`), but it means the two functions' notion of \"installed\" doesn't match the directory search `systemdServiceFiles` actually performs. Is this early short-circuit intentional, or should the not-installed check also go through `systemdServiceFiles`?",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-27T17:19:15Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": "2026-10-27T18:23:05Z",
                    "url": "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4230#note_4101192900",
                    "system": false,
                    "internal": false,
                    "author": {
                      "username": "GitLabDuo",
                      "name": "GitLab Duo",
                      "avatarUrl": "/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836",
                      "bot": true
                    },
                    "position": {
                      "filePath": "internal/commands/govern/internal/fallbacksync/fallbacksync.go",
                      "newLine": 426,
                      "oldLine": null
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "gid://gitlab/DiffNote/4101662832",
                    "body": "Yes, intentional. glab only writes its unit to `~/.config/systemd/user`, so `readJob` first checks that glab's own file is there.\n\nWhen it is, `systemdServiceFiles` looks through the other unit dirs because systemd applies the highest-priority copy of the unit and its drop-ins on top. That way glab reads the effective `Environment=` value.\n\nA same-named unit that exists only in another directory isn't one glab installed. Setup and doctor should report not installed for it, and setup then installs glab's own. No code change.",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-27T18:23:04Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": "2026-10-27T18:23:05Z",
                    "url": "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4230#note_4101662832",
                    "system": false,
                    "internal": false,
                    "author": {
                      "username": "andrew.jung",
                      "name": "Andrew Jung",
                      "avatarUrl": "/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/23194436/avatar.png?v=1794204719",
                      "bot": false
                    },
                    "position": {
                      "filePath": "internal/commands/govern/internal/fallbacksync/fallbacksync.go",
                      "newLine": 426,
                      "oldLine": null
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "gid://gitlab/Discussion/86f7998238676d73dce7f9f430640591ccd37fdf",
              "resolvable": true,
              "resolved": true,
              "notes": {
                "pageInfo": {
                  "hasNextPage": false
                },
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "id": "gid://gitlab/DiffNote/4101192946",
                    "body": "`installFallbackSync` writes `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` into the job's files without checking it is an absolute path. `claudehooks.CheckConfigDir()` already exists and enforces exactly this (it is called from `doctor.go` for the hooks), but it is not called here before `job.ClaudeConfigDir` is set. A relative `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` would be written into the launchd plist or systemd `Environment=` line, and later read back by `InstalledClaudeConfigDir`, which explicitly errors on a relative value (`\"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is not an absolute path\"`). So the job would silently install with a config dir that glab's own reader considers invalid, and nothing in this code path warns the user at setup time. Should `installFallbackSync` call `claudehooks.CheckConfigDir()` (or equivalently validate `filepath.IsAbs`) before setting `job.ClaudeConfigDir`?",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-27T17:19:16Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": "2026-10-27T18:23:06Z",
                    "url": "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4230#note_4101192946",
                    "system": false,
                    "internal": false,
                    "author": {
                      "username": "GitLabDuo",
                      "name": "GitLab Duo",
                      "avatarUrl": "/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836",
                      "bot": true
                    },
                    "position": {
                      "filePath": "internal/commands/govern/setup/setup.go",
                      "newLine": 557,
                      "oldLine": null
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "gid://gitlab/DiffNote/4101663045",
                    "body": "Good catch. Fixed in 386bdd828 (fix(govern): refuse a relative CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR in setup and uninstall).\n\nSetup and uninstall now call `claudehooks.CheckConfigDir()` first and refuse a relative value before writing anything. Setup stops before it reaches `installFallbackSync`, so the job never gets a relative path. Added `TestRunSetup_RefusesRelativeClaudeConfigDir` and `TestRunUninstall_RefusesRelativeClaudeConfigDir`.\n\nThese checks used to arrive only in https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4196 at the top of the stack. They land here now, and the final code of the stack is the same.",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-27T18:23:06Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": "2026-10-27T18:23:06Z",
                    "url": "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4230#note_4101663045",
                    "system": false,
                    "internal": false,
                    "author": {
                      "username": "andrew.jung",
                      "name": "Andrew Jung",
                      "avatarUrl": "/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/23194436/avatar.png?v=1794204719",
                      "bot": false
                    },
                    "position": {
                      "filePath": "internal/commands/govern/setup/setup.go",
                      "newLine": 557,
                      "oldLine": null
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
